  "chosen": "Candidate 3 is chosen because it directly blocks unsafe VO commands using an inexpensive raw‑TTC check, integrates cleanly with the existing VO pipeline, and addresses the core failure where unmapped points are not represented in VO tracks.",
  "target": "controller (add raw‑TTC gating before _vo_planner) and a small helper function _raw_ttc_gate",
  "direction": "1. Implement _raw_ttc_gate(st, pose) that extracts unmapped points via _unmapped_raw, filters those within a ±30° forward cone, and computes TTC = d / (max(rel_speed,0.1)+_MAX_OBJECT_SPEED). 2. In controller(), after _perceive and before any VO or speed logic, call _raw_ttc_gate; if it returns a pause duration, set st['pause_until']=max(st.get('pause_until',-1.0), t+pause) and return (0.0,0.0,False). 3. While paused, keep the clearance‑hold active (call _arm_clear_hold) so the robot stays stopped. 4. Only when t >= st['pause_until'] and the TTC of all forward points exceeds 1.5 s for 0.5 s, clear the pause flag and resume normal VO/predictive‑speed flow. 5. Ensure _guard is still applied to any backup command issued during the pause. 6. Tune the TTC thresholds (0.8 s for stop, 1.5 s for resume) based on observed closing speeds.",
